# Each record is a concrete, reviewable integration proposal. No candidate is silently accepted.
items=[]
def item(id,priority,topic,loc,origin,finding,compat,change,validation,status='Proposed'):
 items.append(dict(id=id,priority=priority,topic=topic,ethan_reference=loc,attribution=origin,evidence_and_insight=finding,compatibility=compat,proposed_code_or_thesis_change=change,validation=validation,status=status))
item('I01','P0','Configuration/provenance gate','4.1.1 PDF47-49 / print33-35;5.1.1 PDF63-65;5.7 Table5.1 PDF81;A.1-A.3 PDF121-124','Ethan reconstruction; supplier parts, photographs and reported private correspondence, not survey-grade experimental truth','Nominal0.93in pipe ID,21.5deg incline,0.83in test bore,4.353m path,2.00in salt insulation. Cooler nominal1ft differs from262.5mm active mesh segment. Appendix calls right leg riser although body calls it downcomer.','Our Ch3 table loop_summary uses0.87in bore,20deg-style idealization,0.835in 1D quartz bore vs20.94mm CFD,304.8mm jacket,1.40in Calzite. At fixed mass flow density,0.93in has14.27% larger area and12.49% lower velocity; fixed-flow laminar pipe resistance drops23.41%. These are scaling comparisons, not predicted loop changes.','Ch3: add a versioned geometry/material crosswalk. Code: import separate configuration profiles, never overwrite frozen CFD/ROM setup. Record original input hashes and mapping of all junctions/heat patches.','Recover actual mesh/dictionaries behind both studies, compute area/volume/centerline lengths, compare to records and rerun only an isolated geometry sensitivity. Gate any quantitative transfer on reconciliation.','Required before numerical adoption')
item('I02','P0','Property package and dimensionless labels','4.3.1 Eqs4.2-5 PDF52-54;5.2.2 Eqs5.15-18 PDF72;B.1 TableB.1 PDF125;C.2 TableC.3 PDF131','Legacy property laws cited to Janz/Reis; modern viscosity/cp from Jin/Parida; reconstruction and choice are Ethan\'s','Body uses modern exponential mu and1423.47cp, appendix gives legacy polynomials. Published Pr labels31.74-54.29 do not describe modern property package unchanged. Appendix global/local Pr rows also disagree.','Our Ch4 eq:hitec-* already matches body modern package; changing to TableB.1 would regress consistency. Our tabulated CFD transport vs analytic ROM also needs interpolation parity.','Ch2/3/4: identify historical case labels versus recomputed local/global nondimensional numbers and temperature definitions. Code: one versioned property registry plus explicit legacy_reproduction profile; no retuning of frozen P1/P2.','Compare property values and derivatives at measured and solver temperatures; sweep positivity and range; test Kelvin conversion and tabulated interpolation; record units and composition basis. W1/W2/W12.','Required audit; modern package already present')
item('I03','P0','Cylindrical wall heat transfer','3.4 PDF40-43 Fig3.1/Eq3.12;5.4.2 Eqs5.23-25 PDF77-78','Classical annular conduction and radiation; custom rcExternalTemperature implementation is Ethan\'s','Per-inner-area resistance sum r0 ln(ri/ri-1)/ki and external area ratio rout/r0 are essential for thick insulation; no axial wall conduction/storage.','Our Ch2 cylindrical resistances and Ch4 localized wall states already capture key idea. Ethan\'s solid material and thickness values differ, so transfer equations/verification strategy rather than coefficients.','Add explicit area basis and source partition to Ch4; audit implementation q_in*Ain=q_out*Aout. Clarify wall-face vs cell-center Tp. Extend candidate BC tests, not replace current closures.','Constant-k multilayer cylinder, convection-only/radiation-only/mixed, zero source, heater-layer source and limiting cases; compare integrated powers and dimensional residuals. Source p77.','Recommended; partial existing implementation')
item('I04','P0','Air cooler enthalpy correction','5.1.3 Eq5.6 PDF68 / print54;B.3 TableB.4 PDF127','Ethan formula; enthalpy identity is standard thermodynamics','cp(Tout)Tout-cp(Tin)Tin is not integral cp dT. AppendixB coefficients over25-to113C give+2.1408% error; midpoint-cp approximation differs-0.0292%.','Our Ch4 cooler uses effectiveness-NTU and air balance, not automatically the same bug. Inspect actual ROM code before changing it.','Document and implement exact polynomial enthalpy integral where variable cp is used; retain current effectiveness-NTU model and geometry. Add a separate comparator reproducing printed formula for diagnosis only.','Constant-cp limit; analytical polynomial primitive vs quadrature; invariance of enthalpy difference to reference offset; air/fluid cooler heat balance. W3 supports identity.','Recommended conditional correction')
item('I05','P0','Experimental energy consistency','4.5.1 Eqs4.6-8 Tables4.4 PDF55-56;C.1 TableC.1 PDF130','Reis equations/measurements as transcribed; negative-loss reconstruction is Ethan\'s','Table4.4 reports negative inferred salt losses for1-3 under legacy cp; table DeltaT row conflicts with TP6-TP2 from C.1. Corrected-cp diagnostic with reported mdot and C.1 gives208.27,238.43,226.19,194.56W. Those are recalculations, not new measured heat inputs.','Our electrical input37W test section and gross/net wall flux ledger are already explicit. Do not impose this inferred net heat or silently discard cases from our CFD assessment.','Add Ch3 experimental-data caveat and separate measurement table with original/reconstructed columns. Code: control-volume-specific energy ledger; keep electrical vs net deposited power and measurement operators separate.','Reconstruct all eight cases from raw temperatures, powers, mdot processing and cp; propagate full uncertainty; compare reported values without overwriting originals.','Required before citing energy paradox as experiment failure')
item('I06','P0','PIV observation operator versus transport','3.5 PDF43-44;4.5.2 Eqs4.9-10 Table4.5 PDF56-57;6.2 PDF97;6.10 PDF109','Experimental measurement belongs to Reis; right-half axisymmetric reconstruction and<1.3% reproduction are Ethan\'s','Axisymmetric integral from a single planar half-profile is an observational reconstruction; three-dimensional asymmetry/recirculation violates symmetry. Table6.10 explicitly uses piv_method.','Our Ch2 signed mass-flux and net-enthalpy reductions are more appropriate for conservative ROM runtime. Keep them; experimental-proxy agreement does not establish same net loop mdot.','Ch3: label mdot_net, mdot_forward, mdot_reverse and mdot_piv_proxy separately, with density/area/plane/time averaging and symmetry assumptions. Code: optional observation-operator module outside runtime targets.','Apply both operators to identical full CFD fields; integrate signed flux on multiple planes, assess right/left proxy bias and recover raw published PIV where available.','Recommended; do not replace conservative targets')
item('I07','P0','Quantity-specific verification','3.1-3.3 Eqs3.1-11 PDF35-40;6.2 Tables6.6-9 PDF93-98;A.4 PDF124','Richardson/GCI from Roache/Celik; two-grid application is Ethan\'s','Full-loop study completed only coarse/medium; cannot estimate observed p or establish monotonic/asymptotic convergence from two solutions. Table3.1 cell targets differ from A.3 by2x in bulk; mesh counts2.552/8.241/28.614M differ from our2.17M reference.','No imported GCI values apply to our production mesh. Our Ch3 already states mesh-evidence limitations; preserve them.','Add source-specific limitations to Ch3 and Ch5. Code/report: GCI per exact QoI/mesh family with realized h, assumed vs observed p, iterative error and stationarity flags; unavailable estimates remain missing, not zero.','Three settled meshes of same geometry/BC and reduction; grid-independent probes/planes; temporal/iterative error small relative to differences. If only two, publish assumed-order estimate with Fs and assumptions, not demonstrated order. W5/W6.','Required claim boundary')
item('I08','P0','Uncertainty and confidence','3.6 Eq3.15 PDF44;5.7 Tables5.1/2 PDF81-85;6.3 PDF97-98;7.1 PDF113','ASME framework is cited; input bounds/propagation/99% claim are Ethan\'s choices','Uncertainties combine standard input distributions with GCI safety bands; independence and covariance require care. No shown coverage factor establishes99%. Insulation-k and air-flow uncertainty omitted; high fit R2 does not bound extrapolation error.','Our retrospective ROM-to-CFD assessment must not become99%-validated experiment claim by inheritance. Shared CFD/experiment inputs can correlate uncertainties.','Ch5: quantitative uncertainty budget per QoI, standard vs expanded vs bounds and provenance; first-order Jacobian covariance or sensitivity ensembles in separate analysis scripts. Replace generic validated language with error and interval definitions.','Check independent synthetic cases, correlated sensors/shared properties, nonlinear ensemble sensitivity, and withheld cases. W4/W5/W14.','Recommended; no99% claim')
item('I09','P1','Strong sensor-position sensitivity','3.5 PDF43-44;4.2.1 PDF50;6.4 Figs6.10-12 PDF99-103','Experimental nominal probes from Reis; CFD spatial-sensitivity result is Ethan\'s','0.1in (2.54mm) neighborhood around TP3 can change reported temperature by>10K. Wall azimuth is uncertain; TW10 is jacket exterior.','Directly relevant to our probe projections and existing TP2 sensitivity; cannot calibrate internal h to a misregistered sensor.','Ch3: sensor observation-map table including fluid centerline, steel outer wall, jacket wall; augment location and azimuth sensitivity near gradients. Code: fixed coordinate/region operators and uncertainty ensembles, never select best location using test data.','Sample resolved fields in physically justified coordinate bounds, compare local/bulk temperatures, freeze mapping before scoring; report nominal and marginalized errors.','Recommended')
item('I10','P1','Recirculation and thermal stratification','6.4 Figs6.10,6.16-20 PDF102,105-108','Ethan CFD observation; later experimental confirmation is reported private correspondence, not independently documented raw observation','Fast near-wall rising stream and reverse flow in opposite region persist into quartz/test section; complex tee geometry deflects the stream.','Supports our existing two-state momentum/recirculation motivation. It does not identify exchange coefficients or prove a thermal-exchange model improves held-out targets.','Ch3/5: cite source for qualitative mechanism, retain our measured forward/reverse metrics and conservative two-state model. New thermal closure only as hypothesis with same-QoI identification.','Recompute signed cross-section mass and enthalpy budgets, momentum leverage and reverse area on our fields; qualify at own meshes/windows; test withheld powers without refit.','Recommended explanatory integration')
item('I11','P1','Developing-flow length scales','2.1 PDF26-27;3.4.1 PDF41;6.1 Eqs6.1-2 PDF87;3.13 PDF43','Straight-tube textbook estimates; Ethan applies them to this facility','Hydrodynamic and thermal entrance lengths have different coefficients for different development tolerances. In verification Re334/Pr53.2/D20mm gives0.334m and17.77m with0.05 coefficient.','Our Shah entry friction and Muzychka-Yovanovich heat transfer are already developing-flow choices. Junctions, recirculation and heating resets mean no universal single entry coordinate.','Ch2/4: state entry-length definition, tolerance, reset convention and applicable flow assumptions; compare Graetz/Sellars reference only on a straight-tube benchmark.','Fully developed asymptotes; entrance-limit behavior; laminar reference data; never substitute3.657 everywhere or apply Dittus-Boelter at these Re. W7.','Recommended clarification')
item('I12','P1','External convection and orientation','5.1.2 Eqs5.1-5 PDF67-68','Churchill-Chu correlations are cited; sin(theta)^2 blend is Ethan\'s interpolation','Vertical plate Nu_L and horizontal cylinder Nu_D use different characteristic lengths. Eq5.3 writesD generally; combining Nu values would be ambiguous, whereas5.5 blends h.','Our ambient model can use same family, but must check outer diameter, segment length, film air properties, curvature and ambient conditions.','Ch2/4: cite both1975 papers, define characteristic length per correlation, expose blend as assumption. Code: test h_horizontal=Nu_D k/Dout and h_vertical=Nu_L k/L before blending.','Orientation endpoints0/90deg, unit checks, film-property sweep, vertical-cylinder criterion and sensitivity to blend exponent/ambient; do not call interpolation universally validated. W8/W9.','Recommended audit')
item('I13','P1','Fins/stubs and missing heat paths','5.1.4 PDF69 / print55;5.7 PDF82-84','Composite fin model and9-16% inferred loss share are Ethan\'s; geometry partly assumed','Seven cap/valve/off-gas paths modeled as2D axisymmetric solid-core composite fins; solid-core model can overestimate hollow/valve losses.','Relevant to our junction/stub ambient loss terms and localized heat-path model, already present. Percentage and fin conductances cannot transfer across different geometry/insulation.','Add a physically grounded fin candidate to separate structural-loss class, leaving current calibrated coefficients/frozen results intact. Record cap/valve lengths and hollow sections.','Compare analytic fin limits,2D energy conservation, hollow vs solid sensitivity, and independent surface temperatures; identify loss using dedicated data rather than aggregate temperature fit.','Conditional candidate')
item('I14','P1','Heater and quartz source distribution','4.1.1 PDF48;6.5 PDF110-111','Ethan interpretation of experiment; localized heating evidence cited to Reis2024 heater-failure article[24]Fig8','Uniform quartz heating may miss two end rings; local near-wall heat can alter viscosity and velocity-profile development.','Our setup uses37W on quartz. Same total electrical input does not imply same spatial source or deposited-fluid heat.','Ch4/5: label current uniform distribution; propose ring/end-patch sensitivity with preserved total power. No coefficient adjustment until input/source geometry reconciled.','Use documented ring locations/widths or explicit bounds, integrate source to37W, compare profiles/temperature/heat ledger and held-out cases; do not infer rings solely from improved fit.','Conditional experiment')
item('I15','P1','BC verification benchmark independence','3.4 Eq3.12/13 PDF40-43;6.1 Tables6.2-5 PDF86-92;C.3 PDF132','Ethan benchmark uses analytical resistance and empirical developing-film correlation','Mode A/B/C separate convection/radiation. Fine reference errors~0.05-0.07%; however equation3.13 atGz3554 givesNu23.7336 while appendix says26.67. Geometry polygonization raises integrated-Q observed order~2.74-2.98.','Useful test architecture, not evidence our BC implementation/mesh is verified. Our actual layer heat sources and temperature-dependent material treatment need additional tests.','Use independent pure conduction boundary tests with prescribed inner wall temperature first, then fluid-coupled benchmark; repair reference Nu, area and mesh-size bookkeeping before using tolerances.','Separate analytic geometry, meshed geometry and per-area flux vs integrated power; test residual, solution difference and refinement. Do not mistake algebraic qbalance machine precision for model accuracy.','Recommended benchmark redesign')
item('I16','P1','Nonlinear solver and steady-state evidence','5.1.2 PDF68;5.5.1 PDF78-79;5.6 PDF80-81','Ethan implementation choices','Under-relaxation0.5; wall iterations deltaTs<1e-3K/deltaq<1e-2W/m2. CFD pseudo-time Co_max5, terminal100s statistics; no physical transient accuracy claimed.','Our production source states different stationarity windows/tolerances and solver schemes. We can adopt diagnostic philosophy, not those numerical thresholds blindly.','Keep own stationarity gate. Add normalized global energy and loop momentum residuals, root-bracket diagnostics and iteration sensitivity to reduced solver; document actual pseudo-time scheme.','Tighter tolerances, different initial guesses/brackets and multiple terminal windows; timestep sensitivity if fluctuations affect means. Do not interpret solver fluctuations as physical transition without temporal checks.','Recommended diagnostics')
item('I17','P2','Water transition modeling','5.2.3 Eq5.19 PDF73-74;6.2 PDF94;6.4 PDF102,106;Table6.10 PDF109','Ethan exploratory SSTLM/Gb variants; original Reis article reports laminar boundary-layer scaling','Text predictswater3/4 benefit, actual selected best fits usewater2Gb andwater4SSTLM. GlobalRa>1e10 alone is not a universal pipe-loop transition criterion. Local y+ reaches~5.','Current work is laminar HITEC-focused; water turbulence is outside main comparison and cannot justify changing salt closure.','Keep in literature/limitations only. If later extending to water, declare model selection before validation and implement buoyancy source with correct rho normalization.','Independent transition data, model coefficient/source audit, near-wall resolution and actual-time/timestep sensitivity; compare all cases without selecting model post hoc. W10/W12.','Defer outside present scope')
item('I18','P1','Digitized-profile provenance','4.5.3 Figs4.2-4/Tables4.6/7 PDF58-61','Ethan extraction and salt raw-data cross-check; water raw full fields unavailable','Masking/calibration/brightness classification, column median and smoothing; global1.36% RMSE rounded1.5%, but one height3.65% RMS and14.10%max.','Useful if raw PIV cannot be obtained; no need if our target is own CFD fields. Noise/crossing smoothing can bias profiles.','Add digitization workflow only for external experimental comparison; store source image, calibration points, smoothing and profiles with pointwise quality flags.','Overlay digitized result, blind validation on available raw salt data, per-case/per-height uncertainty and endpoint sensitivity. Do not apply1.5% as guaranteed pointwise bound.','Conditional supporting analysis')
item('I19','P0','Salt1 evidence handling','6.5 PDF110-111;TableC.1 PDF130;Table6.10 PDF109','Ethan suspects label/entry/configuration mismatch; not a demonstrated correction to original experiment','Salt1 mean-fluid error-24.43K and proxy-mdot error-28.18%. TW10 Salt1 exceedsSalt2 by0.36K, smaller than stated1.56K difference uncertainty; that observation alone cannot establish faulty data.','Our Salt1 CFD development case is distinct from a questionable experiment label. Do not remove or reclassify our case by name alone.','Ch3/5: mark suspected experimental inconsistency unresolved; report with/without sensitivity only when same underlying measurements are identified. Preserve all original values and labels.','Trace run IDs/powers/heating/airflow/insulation to raw experimental records; compare uncertainty-normalized differences; no confirmed fault statement without documentary evidence.','Required wording restriction')
item('I20','P0','Result interpretation and calibration','Table6.10 PDF109;6.4 PDF99,106;5.7 PDF82;7.1 PDF113','Ethan results and post hoc choices','Seven non-Salt1 aggregate case verdicts lie inside adopted bands. Wall values use best-aligned azimuth; water2/4 use selected turbulence models; water insulation effective 0.40 in was adjusted for fit. These are retrospective comparisons.','Our thesis title already says retrospective model assessment, and target-informed P2-CFD is identified. Ethan\'s table does not upgrade our CFD-driven ROM to experimental predictive validation.','Ch3/5/6: separate calibration/reconstruction, solution verification, experimental comparison and ROM-to-CFD assessment. Cite Table6.10 as reported under its assumptions, not validated universal truth.','Freeze configuration/measurement operator/model before withheld data; recompute per-probe/profile errors, coverage and case aggregates; no best-of-model scoring presented as prospective performance. W5.','Required claim boundary')
item('I21','P1','Insulation and material properties','4.1.2 PDF49;5.7 PDF82-84;B.4 TablesB.5 PDF127,unnumbered k PDF128','Ethan manufacturer-fit and extrapolation; SS/quartz engineering constants','Ceramic fit differs from our Calzite/ceramic input; appendix typo6.4209E-0.2; aluminum epsilon0.10 inTable5.1 vs0.15 inB.5. Insulation-fit R2=0.998 does not establish room-temperature accuracy.','Do not replace our temperature-dependent SS316L/current insulation coefficients with Ethan\'s constant16.3W/mK steel or different ceramic fit.','Ch4: cite actual manufacturer/material identity and fit range, record extrapolation uncertainty. Code: registry with provenance/validity, exact coefficient digits, source-specific emissivity.','Sweep actual wall/insulation temperatures; compare source datasheet points, positivity, uncertainty and sensitivity. Require new evidence before changing material package.','Recommended provenance audit')
item('I22','P2','Automated CFD pipeline and mesh quality','5.3/5.6 PDF74-81;A.3 TablesA.4/5 PDF124','Ethan foam-vv/classy_blocks/Jinja orchestration; software utilities are cited','Structured conformal O-grids, coarse-to-medium mapping and diagnostic extraction aid reproducibility. Hexahedral mesh is not by itself proof of smaller error than every polyhedral alternative.','Reusable workflow pattern; actual source repo and YAMLs are not included in PDF or our manuscript ZIP.','Request/locate exact foam-vv commit/config files when implementation begins. Add manifest/provenance/quality-gate design; do not rebuild framework from prose without necessity.','Reproduce one case from frozen manifest; mesh quality checks plus QoI sensitivity and parallel consistency.','Defer code adoption until source available')
item('I23','P0','Bibliography and source version','Title PDF1;references[48][50][51] PDF119-120;our references.bib keyrozak2026cfdNaturalCirculation','Direct bibliographic comparison','Uploaded title beginsHigh-Fidelity CFD Simulation... and title page saysMay2026; our bib entry uses reversed title,aug and Forthcoming. PDF metadata creationAug2026 does not prove degree/title month. Santini entry prints1948 instead of1984; Jin author list omitsXuehuiAn.','Safe documentation edits once selected; do not invent repository DOI/URL or claim published status.','Update existing Rozak key to exact supplied title, year, and note that supplied manuscript title page saysMay2026; confirm month before bibliographic finalization. Add distinct Churchill-Chu horizontal entry. Verify all reused original-source metadata.','BibTeX uniqueness/build, titles/DOIs against primary publishers, citation resolution and scientific-claim guardrails.','Recommended documentation change')
item('I24','P1','Preserve model hierarchy and agreement gates','Ethan7.2 PDF113;comparison to our Ch4/5','Integration judgment based on both sources','Much of Ethan\'s radial physics, modern salt properties, energy ledger and recirculation motivation is already in our manuscript. Highest value is provenance, operator and uncertainty repair.','Retain P1, P2-baseline naming preference, P2-CFD target-informed scale and frozen train/test split. Source ZIP still usesP2-unity in one table; user\'s later preference controls name when editing is agreed.','Implement selected documentation changes first, observation/verification tooling second, physical variants last. No numeric tables updated until reproducible reruns are available.','Run repository compile_and_qa and affected scientific guardrails; reproduce baseline results before/after code changes and report any altered result explicitly.','Plan only; awaiting agreed scope')
save('integration_plan',items)

