intro='''<h1>Ethan’s thesis → your CFD-to-1D thesis</h1><p><b>Evidence-backed integration plan · 20 October2026 · review edition</b></p><p>The strongest integration is to make your computational reference more traceable: reconcile configuration versions, distinguish the PIV observation operator from conservative transport, strengthen the wall/energy verification, and qualify uncertainty and validation claims. Ethan’s radial heat-transfer laws, modern HITEC properties, and recirculation motivation are largely already present in your manuscript. Importing his numerical validation labels without reconciling the configurations would weaken your scientific argument.</p><div class="warn"><b>Scope:</b> This is a plan and extraction package, not a manuscript or production-code update. Proposed integrations I01-I24 remain reviewable. No new experimental results, calibrated coefficients or CFD results are asserted. Numerical recalculations below diagnose the supplied text and are not reruns of Ethan’s software.</div><nav><a href="Equation_Inventory.html">61 equations +31 unnumbered groups</a><a href="Image_Atlas.html">33 figures +39 native images</a><a href="data/integration_plan.csv">Integration CSV</a><a href="data/fact_checks.csv">Fact-check CSV</a><a href="Full_Text.txt">Full text</a><a href="Ethan_Rozak_Thesis_Original.pdf">Original PDF</a></nav><h2>Evidence boundaries</h2><p>The supplied PDF has139 pages; body printed page3 begins atPDF17. For the numbered body/appendices, printed page=PDFpage−14. Both systems are retained in each inventory. The139 page images preserve every source page, including unnumbered/inline equations and vector graphics; a semantic claim that every inline algebraic fragment has been individually classified is not made. All61 numbered displays were located and their page contexts visually inspected;31 unnumbered groups also capture the main definitions, closures, coefficient tables and duplicate/malformed formulas. Tables and raw text remain in the package.</p><p>Your comparison baseline is the current uploaded CSEM_Master_s_Dissertation(7)(2).zip, whose README calls it the six-chapter source. The active Ch3/Ch4 inputs and existing limitations control this assessment. Its source snapshot is provided for audit inReference_Thesis_Source.zip; it is not an authoritative new upstream version. The ZIP does not include the complete executable CFD/ROM simulation archive. The assessment therefore specifies code behavior and tests rather than inventing exact runtime module paths.</p><h2>What should change first</h2><ol><li><b>Required before quantitative adoption:</b> I01/I02configuration and property provenance; I05/I06energy and measurement operators; I07/I08verification and uncertainty; I19/I20claim boundaries.</li><li><b>Recommended first implementation scope:</b> documentation/provenance corrections, existing-model wall/enthalpy diagnostics, and a source-linked comparison appendix. Keep numerical results and frozen model definitions unchanged until rerun evidence supports a change.</li><li><b>Conditional physical candidates:</b> finite structural-loss paths, quartz end-ring heating, sensor location ensembles and nonuniform external convection. Identify against the same quantities used to score them and test frozen coefficients on withheld cases.</li><li><b>Deferred:</b> water-transition closures and a wholesale foam-vv pipeline rewrite.</li></ol><h2>Configuration crosswalk</h2>'''
